Not at present.

> 2. Is the kinship matrix recommended for analysis of an F2 population? Or is this more suited for RILs like the Collaborative Cross?
>

Use of a linear mixed model with a polygenic effect for background QTL is potentially useful in an F2 and not just in populations with some structure. But the "best" analysis likely depends on the (unknown) genetic architecture of the trait.

> 3. I noticed that the legends for QTL effect plots depend on the order that the alleles are listed in the yaml file. I want to confirm that I've listed mine in the correct order. In my yaml I have this information:
>
