Hi Karl,

Thanks for the reply.

We tried the way you suggested as masking small probability as 0s, it still did not solve the problem.

As suggested by Dan Gatti, we calculated the probability in R/qtl, and changed the format into R/qtl2, so we can’t simply use clean_genopro. What we did was masking all the small values (< 0.001) into 0 as in the processing of formatting change. And we double checked the probability of each chromosome, and the small probability values have been changed to 0s. it still produced wired values with scan1coef and plot_coef.

Another thing is when we ran scan1coef, we set se = TRUE, but the output doesn’t have any information about standard error.

